The shibboleth module lets nginx delegate authentication to a Shibboleth
service provider.  It turns the answer of an authorization subrequest into
the request headers that the protected application expects, so a FastCGI
backend sees the same attributes it would see behind Apache.

A running shibd and its FastCGI responders are needed separately; the module
only speaks to them.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built by
the nginx ports when their SHIBBOLETH option is enabled.
